{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>And he shall administer the oath.</b> That he say to her that she accept upon herself the oath of the imprecation under this condition." "<b>If you have not lain.</b> Now." "<b>And if you have not gone astray in defilement.</b> At other times." "<b>You are cleared.</b> Since it was already stated: כִּי לֹא יְנַקֶּה ה׳ אֵת אֲשֶׁר יִשָּׂא אֶת שְׁמוֹ לַשָּׁוְא (Exodus 20:7), so that even if a person swears to the truth in the oath of imprecation, if the matter is unnecessary — like one who swears to that which is already known — the swearer does not escape the imprecation. You, who caused the matter to become doubtful to us and obligated yourself in this oath, would deserve that even if you swear to the truth you would not be cleared. Nevertheless, I accept the imprecations on this condition: that you are cleared from them if you have not gone astray."], :book :numbers, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 5, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:38:45.794763877Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}